WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.766 --> 00:00:03.036 line:0%
- FREE AT LAST,
FREE AT LAST,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.670 line:0%
THANK GOD ALMIGHTY,

00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:06.205 line:0%
WE ARE FREE AT LAST.

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:11.511 line:0%
[cheers and applause]

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.049 line:0%
- LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
PLEASE WELCOME

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.618 line:0%
YOUR NEXT SPEAKER,
THE REVEREND ROBERT JONES.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.388 line:0%
[moderate applause]

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:28.828 line:0%
- [whispers]
HOW AM I S'POSED TO FOLLOW THAT?

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:31.330 line:0%
I CAN'T.
NOBODY CAN FOLLOW THAT.

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:32.832 line:0%
HOW AM I S--

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:35.134
I CAN, UH...

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.136
OH.
[feedback]

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.571
ALL RIGHT.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:39.705
[shrill feedback]

00:00:39.738 --> 00:00:43.376
GOOD AFTERNOON.
UM...

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.811
THAT--THAT IS THE--

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.747
THE BEST SPEECH I'VE EVER HEARD
IN MY ENTIRE LIFE.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.383
[chuckles]
EVER.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.518
I HAVE NEVER HEARD
A BETTER SPEECH.

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:54.287
[chuckles]

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.824
AND NOW IT IS MY TURN
TO SPEAK.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:01.194
HUH.
[chuckles and stammers]

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.162
WHO PUT THIS RUNNING ORDER
TOGETHER, RIGHT?

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:06.466
YOU KNOW, UM,
DR. KING, UH,

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.634
HE--HE ACTUALLY COVERED
A LOT--

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.403
A LOT OF WHAT
I WAS GONNA SAY.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.306
UM, YOU KNOW, MY--
MY SPEECH IS, UH, UH--

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.707
YOU GONNA
FIND THIS FUNNY, Y'ALL.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.876
MY SPEECH
WAS ACTUALLY CALLED, UH,

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.278
"A VISION FOR THE FUTURE."

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.180
I'M NOT SAYING THAT DR. KING
COPIED MY SPEECH.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:22.515
I'M--
[crowd murmurs]

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.617
NO! NO!
NO, I'M--I'M--

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.352
I'M SAYING
I'M NOT SAYING THAT.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:28.454
I'M NOT SAYING
HE TRIED TO COPY IT.

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:30.590
YOU--WHY DON'T Y'ALL LISTEN
TO WHAT I'M S--

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.558
[murmuring intensifies]
WOW. YOU KNOW WHAT?

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:33.693
[crowd booing]
NO, COME ON!

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.828
I'M JUST SAYING.
I'M JUST SAYING.

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.131
I'M JUST SAYING.
IT'S A JOKE.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.533
DID I NOT SAY IT
LIKE A JOKE?

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.835
OK--

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.471
NO?

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.874
APPARENTLY,
I HAVE SIX MORE MINUTES.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.742 line:0%
HE, UH, GOT THAT OUT THERE.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.811 line:0%
[chuckles]

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.312 line:0%
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:54.313
ALL RIGHT, HERE--
HERE'S SOMETHING--

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:55.515
HERE'S SOMETHING NEW.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.849
HERE'S SOMETHING BRAND NEW.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.484
HOW--OKAY, THIS IS OFF--

00:01:58.517 --> 00:01:59.785
ME TALKING OFF THE TOP
OF MY HEAD HERE, EVERYBODY.

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:03.756
UH, WHAT--HOW ABOUT
IF WE LET, UH, BLACK PEOPLE

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.591
ENSLAVE WHITE PEOPLE FOR--
[crowd boos]

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:07.260
OKAY, YOU KNOW,
THAT SOUNDED A LOT BETTER

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.661
IN MY HEAD
BEFORE I SAID IT.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:11.230
[booing continues]
SO THAT, UH,

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:12.798
THAT WOULDN'T WORK.

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:14.233
IS IT WARM?

00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:17.236
IS ANYBODY ELSE WARM?

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:20.640
WHOO!

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.508
- OKAY, OKAY, OKAY.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:23.476
HERE'S WHAT WE GONNA DO.
HERE'S WHAT WE GONNA DO.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.711 line:0%
ALL RIGHT, DR. KING
TALKED ABOUT, UM, UH,

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:27.246 line:0%
ALL THE RACES COMING TOGETHER,
RIGHT? RIGHT?

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:30.249 line:0%
SO WHAT I WANT EVERY NEGRO
TO DO HERE TODAY

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.885 line:0%
IS FIND THE NEAREST WHITE PERSON
AND GIVE 'EM A HUG.

00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:34.487
JUST--JUST GIVE 'EM
A HUG, OKAY?

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.489
NO, SIR,
YOU'RE NOT BEING ATTACKED.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.324
YOU'RE NOT BEING ATTACKED.
YOU'RE BEING HUGGED, OKAY?

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:39.592
EVERYBODY TAKE IT EASY HERE,
OKAY?

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:41.360
EVERYBODY RELAX.
YOU KNOW WHAT?

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:43.796
WE DON'T NEED TEN NEGROES
HUGGING ONE WHITE PERSON, OKAY?

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:46.199
LET'S JUST--LET'S--
YOU KNOW, THAT'S THE NEW RULE.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.234
NOT TEN ON ONE.
ONE ON ONE.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.669
SO WE'LL JUST TAKE TURNS
AND EVERYTHING, OKAY?

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.237
SO EVERYBODY RELAX, OKAY?
[crowd shouting]

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.471
[glass shatters]
OH, MY GOODNESS.

00:02:52.504 --> 00:02:54.407
SIR, SHE DOESN'T NEED
TO BE DEFENDED.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.741
SHE DOESN'T NEED TO BE DEFENDED.
SHE'S OKAY.

00:02:55.774 --> 00:02:56.943
SHE'S OKAY, OKAY?
[crowd screaming]

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.544
ALL RIGHT, MA'AM--OKAY--

00:02:58.577 --> 00:02:59.979
OFFICER,
IS THAT NECESSARY?

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.681
I DON'T THINK
THAT'S NECESSARY, OFFICER.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.249
[sirens wail, horse whinnies]
NO, MA'AM, PLEASE!

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.383
[dogs bark, women scream]
PLEASE TAKE IT EASY, SIR!

00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:05.484
EVERYONE TAKE IT EASY,
ALL RIGHT?

00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:07.220
THEY'RE JUST HUGS.
YOU'RE NOT BEING ATTACKED.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:11.424
[loud screams, sirens wailing]

